    "title": "Christian Apologetics: Who Needs It? - William Lane Craig",
    "video_id": "KDH-_4vkKUk"
   },
   {
    "context": "They will criticize the churches that are too textual, and also the churches that are too spiritual, without understanding that the only reason they're too spiritual is because they're basing it off of how textual they were. And then he goes and he does it himself. He ends with like three Bible verses that we can take truth from. Because at the end of the day, there is nothing else. The only reason you even know the name Jesus is not because the wind whispered it to you. It's because there were written accounts. It's because the Bible was put together and put in front of you and claimed that it contained truth.",
    "dist": 0.4197,
    "occurrence_id": 114589,
    "published_at": "2024-02-13T15:00:51Z",
    "role": "host",
    "surface": "truth",
    "t": 2378.08,
    "title": "Deconstruction Research: Why Do Some People Lose Their Faith While Others Keep It?",
    "video_id": "qaCcrogCNRw"
   },
   {
    "context": "We know what the truth is. We know there's a God, we know there's a creator God, we know there's a moral God. It's written on our hearts, but we suppress that because we want to do our own thing. You can't know anything for sure. Whenever you're right, you're just borrowing from my worldview. You just want to sin, you're suppressing the truth. These are but a few among the charges of heresy, leveled at every non-believer. But regardless of who's doing it, these tactics serve only to obfuscate, not to illuminate.",
